sub:assertion {
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/wolfram2002-ch03-17> delphi:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/wolfram2002-ch03-17--grok> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/wolfram2002-ch03-17--grok> a delphi:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Grok 4.7 on wolfram2002-ch03-17: resolvable-now, resolvability 0.77" ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.2.0> ;
    delphi:assessmentType "dataset-resolvability/0.2.0" ;
    delphi:hasScore "0.77"^^xsd:double ;
    delphi:hasVerdict "resolvable-now" ;
    dct:type "resolution-route/computation" ;
    delphi:hasConfidence "0.76"^^xsd:double ;
    dct:description "The claim is an existence claim about a fully specified class of rewrite systems, and both the rules in the book and a wider sample of short rules can be rerun exactly. Non-stabilizing growth together with a failed periodicity check is a direct confirming outcome, and universal stabilization in the searched class would refute it. The only soft spot is how strongly a finite sample supports 'often,' which is not required to settle the stated 'can.'" ;
    rdfs:comment "Proposed test with existing data: Enumerate small combinator-style rules of the form e[x_][y_] to an expression in x and y, iterate them from a fixed seed, and record whether expression size stabilizes, becomes periodic or nested, or keeps growing while passing randomness tests. A single non-stabilizing, statistically irregular example confirms the claim; every small rule stabilizing or becoming nested would refute it inside that rule bound." ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-grok-4.7-high-fast> ;
    delphi:evidenceAgainst "Visual or statistical irregularity does not prove that a particular rule never eventually stabilizes.", "The frequency word 'often' depends on how the space of expressions is enumerated." ;
    delphi:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/wolfram2002-ch03-17--grok--dataset-1>, <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/wolfram2002-ch03-17--grok--dataset-2> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/wolfram2002-ch03-17--grok--operationalizability> a delphi:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Operationalizability of wolfram2002-ch03-17 by Grok 4.7: 0.7" ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.2.0-operationalizability> ;
    delphi:assessmentType "dataset-resolvability/0.2.0/operationalizability" ;
    delphi:hasScore "0.7"^^xsd:double ;
    dct:isPartOf <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/wolfram2002-ch03-17--grok> ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-grok-4.7-high-fast> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/wolfram2002-ch03-17> delphi:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/wolfram2002-ch03-17--grok--operationalizability> .
